course: dictionary
lesson: 11922
title: Calculated
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Calculated» has more than one meaning, so the clues around it matter. In maths, it means you worked something out with numbers. «We calculated the total cost of the shopping» tells you about adding up prices.
explain: In a story, the same word means something planned. «The thief made a calculated move and left before the guard came back.» The word move and the timing show that the thief planned it carefully, not by luck.
explain: To choose the right meaning, ask: is there a sum or a number? Then it is probably the maths meaning. Is someone planning something carefully? Then it is the planned meaning. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it.
fact: «Calculated» can mean worked out using numbers, as in «We calculated the area.»
fact: «Calculated» can also mean carefully planned to get a result, often in a sneaky way, as in «a calculated lie».
fact: «A calculated risk» is a risk you take after thinking carefully about the chances.
fact: «Calculated» can mean meant or likely to do something, as in «a joke calculated to make him laugh».
fact: Calculate is the base word, and calculates, calculating and calculated are all forms of it.
exercise: «We calculated the total cost of the shopping.» What does calculated mean here? | Carefully planned to trick someone | Thrown away | Meant to make people laugh | *Worked out using numbers
exercise: «The thief made a calculated move and left before the guard came back.» What does calculated suggest? | *Carefully planned | Loud and messy | Accidental, by luck | Wet and cold
exercise: Mia took a calculated risk and jumped in after she checked how deep the water was. What does calculated risk mean? | A sum about how far you can jump | A risk that makes you laugh | *A risk taken after thinking about the chances | A risk taken without any thought
test: «Show how you calculated the answer.» What does calculated mean in this sentence? | Painted in bright colours | Shouted loudly | *Worked out using numbers | Lost in the sums
test: «The joke was calculated to make him laugh.» What does calculated mean in this sentence? | Thrown together by accident | *Meant or likely to make him laugh | Lost on the way home | Written down in a book
exam: «The villain told a calculated lie that fooled the whole town.» What does calculated mean here? | Loud and long | Accidental | Tiny and hard to see | *Carefully planned to fool people
